{"point":{"id":"composition","title":"Application Composition and Transports","rationale":"The server bootstrap selects concrete repositories, agent runtimes, and services, connects their ports, and disposes their resources. The Vite adapter mounts HTTP and WebSocket interfaces. Architecture tests enforce the domain/application/infrastructure/UI boundaries, making this the clearest entry point for understanding dependency direction.","sourcePaths":["src/server/app/bootstrap.ts","src/server/app/vitePlugin.ts","src/server/routes/core/routes.ts","src/server/routes/mapping/routes.ts","src/app/App.tsx","src/app/services.ts","tests/architecture/dependencies.test.ts"],"relationships":[{"pointId":"persistence","label":"constructs and injects filesystem repositories","kind":"ownership"},{"pointId":"agent_access","label":"wires canvas bridges and mounts agent transports","kind":"ownership"},{"pointId":"chat","label":"constructs chat service and disposes its connection","kind":"ownership"},{"pointId":"evals","label":"connects generation, comparison, and experiment services","kind":"ownership"}]},"sources":[{"path":"src/server/app/bootstrap.ts","text":"import { ExperimentService, type StoredExperiment } from '../../../application/mapping/evals/experimentService';
